<title>USA: Owens-Illinois to buy Italy's.</title>
<headline>Owens-Illinois to buy Italy's.</headline>
<dateline>TOLEDO, Ohio 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Owens-Illinois Inc said it will buy a 76 percent stake in AVIR SpA, Italy's largest maker of glass containers, and start a tender offer for the 21 percent stake of AVIR shares that are publically held.</p>
<p>Total cost of all AVIR shares will be about $100 million, Owens-Illinois said.  The acquisition -- expected to close in the first quarter of 1997 -- will boost Owens-Illinois' annual revenue by about $600 million, Owens-Illinois said.</p>
<p>It will make a positive contribution to the company's earnings by 1997, Owens-Illinois added, although did not say by how much.</p>
